course: dictionary
lesson: 870
title: Billboard: a board, a magazine, a chart
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A billboard is a very large board beside a road, or on the side of a building, that shows adverts. Drivers see it for only a moment as they pass, so billboards use big pictures and few words.
explain: Context helps here. «The US Billboard Hot 100 counts sales, streams and radio plays.» The capital B and the words «Hot 100» tell you Billboard is a name, not just a board. It is the name of a magazine that publishes music charts.
explain: When you meet «number one on the Billboard Hot 100», try your meaning in the sentence: the most popular song on that chart. «Mariah Carey's song first reached number one on the Billboard Hot 100 in December 2019, 25 years later.» The clue «25 years later» shows the chart is a list that songs can climb up, and that the song was not number one when it first came out.
fact: A billboard is a very large board for adverts, beside a road or on a building.
fact: Billboards use big pictures and few words, because drivers read them quickly.
fact: In UK English a billboard is also called a hoarding.
fact: Billboard (US) is also the name of a magazine that publishes music charts.
fact: «Number one on the Billboard Hot 100» means the most popular song in the USA on that chart.
exercise: What is a billboard? | A sign only for trains | A small card in a shop window | A type of boat | *A very large board beside a road or on a building, showing adverts
exercise: «The US Billboard Hot 100 counts sales, streams and radio plays.» What is Billboard in this sentence? | A kind of guitar | A road sign for lorries | A band | *A magazine that publishes music charts
exercise: What do people in the UK often call a billboard? | A trolley | *A hoarding | A bus shelter | A kennel
test: Why do billboards use big pictures and few words? | Because they are cheaper to print | Because the board is too small for words | So people can read them while they sit at home | *So drivers can read them quickly as they pass
test: «BTS became the first K-pop act to reach number one on the Billboard Hot 100.» What does number one mean here? | The first song ever written | *The most popular song on the chart | A band with one member | The biggest sign on the road
exam: Which clue in «reached number one on the Billboard Hot 100 in December 2019, 25 years later» tells you a song can climb the chart? | *The word reached, which shows a song moving up to the top | The number 25 on its own | The word December | The year 2019
